{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"agent_message","text":"The main height is **338 mm**. The long shell is **Ø156 outside / Ø150 inside**, giving a **3 mm wall**.\n\nI’ve locked the dimension table as follows:\n\n| Feature | Printed dimensions / interpretation |\n|---|---|\n| Lower flange | Ø210; 8 mm plate; four mounting pads reach 18 mm above the base |\n| Lower mounting pattern | 4 × M8×0.75 through, Ø210 PCD, at 45°, 135°, 225°, 315° |\n| Upper mounting pattern | 6 × M8×0.75, Ø176 PCD; angular positions from the 25°, 52°, 65°, 67.3°, and 22.7° callouts |\n| Shell and upper rim | Base to rim underside 308; base to rim top 338 |\n| Radial ports | Ends 120 and 130 from the main axis; Ø40 callouts; 52-wide square boss; M30×0.7 on the smaller port |\n| External vertical conduit | Ø22; upper transition at height 281 |\n| Lower web | Ø30 central bore; three curved windows; R35/R72 boundaries with R8 corners; construction radii R43/R64 |\n| Web hole pattern | Six small holes; outer locations on Ø134; undimensioned small-hole diameter remains an assumption |\n| Blends | R1 typical at ports, R5 at square-boss corners, R8 at flange/lug transitions |\n\nThe stacked dimensions use the bottom mating face as Z=0:\n\n- **338 overall = 8 lower plate + 300 shell span + 30 upper rim.** The 308 dimension ends at the rim underside; 338 ends at its top.\n- **18 pad height = 8 plate + 10 raised pad.**\n- **334** ends at the port’s upper shoulder, **313** at the smaller port axis, and **281** at the conduit’s upper transition. These are elevations from the base, not additional heights.\n- The smaller 296/285 elevations describe local port steps. They do not increase the 338 mm envelope.\n\nThe handle radius, web thickness, and small-hole diameter are not explicitly dimensioned; I’ll keep those as separate assumed parameters.\n"}}
